<urn:atm:triage:finding/RBP-F001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBP-F001" ;
  triage:title "TaskStore escalation-recipient surface represents addresses as unvalidated String/&str at the trait boundary" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr QA-1 (rust-best-practices-agent), PR #1408 @ 5ab184d75, https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1408#issuecomment-5642703785. The TaskStore trait's escalation-recipient surface (crates/atm-storage/src/task_store.rs:117-140: list_escalation_recipients, add_escalation_recipient, remove_escalation_recipient, effective_escalation_recipients) represents recipient addresses as raw String/&str with zero validation at the trait boundary, even though every other domain id in the same trait is a validated newtype. atm_core::address::AgentAddress already exists and is parsed ad hoc only at the point of use (herdr_escalation.rs:291). fenix's ruling: predates Phase BA (AX.6, 490a6c42a); BA.6 fold-in list." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ba" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "best-practices" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-storage/src/task_store.rs" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T01:58:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "fenix's BA.4 QA-1 ruling (https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1408#issuecomment-5642738654) folds this into BA.6, not BA.4. Further promoted by fenix's cleanup ruling (ATM 2026-09-12T04:44:29Z): worktree layer 5, fix/phase-ba-cleanup (new gh-stack layer above docs/ba6, cipher single writer) -- arch-ctm's BA6-CLEANUP task is cancelled; fix lands once on the cleanup layer, not on docs/ba6." ;
  triage:promoteTo "fix/phase-ba-cleanup-b" ;
  triage:deferredNote "further re-promoted (ATM 2026-09-12T04:51:28Z): docs/ba6-task-nudge-documentation complete and FROZEN at 03c623717 (PR #1412); new layer 6, fix/phase-ba-cleanup-b (arch-ctm single writer), above fix/phase-ba-cleanup (cipher). Rebase-at-task-start is now the rule on every layer -- headSha values in these records are snapshots, not live pointers." ;
  triage:deferredNote "fenix (ATM 01M2A25E8T4QXDAG7FH85MCWF8, 2026-09-12T05:41:38Z): all four cleanup-b findings (RBP-F001, RBP-F002, RSH-001, RBQA-BA5-F004) are now fixed on fix/phase-ba-cleanup-b. FIXED." ;
  triage:deferredNote "fenix (ATM 01M2A33J3NNYGRTMQBDCS1XG4F, 2026-09-12T05:58:05Z): fix/phase-ba-cleanup-b rebased onto c571ae930 and ACCEPTED at a2da4a570 (arch-ctm BA-CLEANUP-B-REBASE-1789191942; ten-gate run green). Fixed occurrence now lives at 5de837a0c (also carries two AgentAddress fixture adaptations from the BA.3 merge); layer frozen. Consolidated QA dispatched as BA-TOP-QA-1789192584 on PR #1414 head a2da4a570 vs base 03c623717." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BA6 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-12T01:58:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
